Here's a patch, inspired by a Slash'EM-ism, that adds yet another
anachronism into the game: pills.

It differs from Slash'EM in that instead of one "pill" item with a
randomly chosen identity upon consumption, there are instead ten pills
(with shuffled colouration) with fixed identities.

* Wishing pills are (supposed to be) very rare. Unlike the others,
they'll never pour forth from horns of plenty.
* Antibiotics pills cure sickness. Maybe save them for your battle with
Demogorgon?
* Vitamin pills increase a random statistic that isn't Charisma.
* Speed pills haste you.
* Headache pills heal (if not cursed) or harm (if cursed) 2d6 hp.
* Earthquake pills have a seismic effect on one's body when swallowed.
* Hallucination pills make the game more interesting to watch.
* Sleeping pills temporarily cure insomnia.
* Placebos give you a message designed to make you misidentify them as
a useful (or dangerous) pill.
* Cyanide capsules kill you unless you are poison resistant.
Also:
*Healers begin in possession of d4 headache pills and d4 antibiotics
pills.
*Nurses and attendants are sometimes generated with 3-5 headache pills.

*The colouration of the pills is supposed to be a reference to Dr.
Mario.

